HEADLINE (non-reactive, 2.0 s lookahead): 28.8% of collisions were INEVITABLE.

READ: most collisions WERE avoidable given perfect knowledge. The
  ceiling is a POLICY limitation, not a kinematic one. A control-layer
  method (CBF-QP, MPC shielding) has genuine headroom -- this is the
  evidence that would justify spending GPU time on it.
